## Direct PMP22 counter-screen

VU0494372 at 10 uM for 16 h gives PMP22 surface geometric fold 0.932, with unpaired log-Welch 95% model interval [0.731, 1.189], n=3 per arm. Total fold is 0.906; efficiency fold 1.046. No improvement is demonstrated, but this is not proof of no effect/equivalence. All single-observation omissions keep the surface point estimate below one; model uncertainty still permits a moderate increase.

The better-matched transient KCNQ1 S4A surface fold is 1.286. The PMP22-minus-KCNQ1 log2 interaction is -0.464, model interval [-0.866, -0.061] if all four groups are independent. Unknown cross-cargo/cross-arm covariance invalidates treating that assumption as established: a covariance sensitivity envelope includes zero. Crucially, PMP22 effects already entered compound selection; this counter-screen is not independent specificity validation. The caption says 0.1% DMSO while both native S4 worksheets say 0.2%; neither label is silently repaired.

All five selected KCNQ1 compound contrasts and WT/coding-variant responses are in candidate-contrast-table.tsv, with endpoints kept separate. They do not establish PMP22 rescue. KCNQ1 cell currents are orthogonal same-study evidence, not matched to surface measurements or transferable myelin function. Supplemental Table 2 and native current counts disagree in three control arms; all native numbers are retained, not trimmed to force agreement. At 20 uM the separate viability panel is lower than vehicle, providing an additional context restriction.

